{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "ReplyNodes App Store Public Reads",
    "version": "v1",
    "summary": "Read-only App Store API for iOS app metadata and ASO research through the ReplyNodes prepaid-credit fetcher.",
    "description": "Machine-readable specification for the supported public App Store read capabilities of the ReplyNodes fetcher domain.\n\nSurface status:\n- All nine reviewed public read methods are exposed as stable capability identifiers in the manifest: app, list, search, developer, privacy, suggest, similar, reviews, and ratings.\n- Each route uses the provider method name and exact option names; app-shaped results are normalized into the public App contract and raw provider records never cross the public gateway.\n- No availability, uptime, latency, or success-rate figure is claimed; example payloads are illustrative fixtures.\n- Package access uses prepaid credits only: one long-lived fetcher key is sent as Authorization: Bearer YOUR_FETCHER_KEY\n\nRead-only guarantees:\n- Every cataloged operation is an HTTP GET capability over public application data only.\n- No purchase, review-submission, account, login, or any other write or authenticated capability exists in this domain, now or later; it is excluded by policy rather than by configuration.\n- Operations can only be disabled at runtime (APPSTORE_FETCHER_DISABLED_OPERATIONS kill switch), never enabled beyond this matrix.\n- No request path carries or accepts credentials, keys, or login material of any kind; the read layer performs public reads server-side.\n- Only public platform data is returned; counters, scores, and prices are null when the source omits them - zeros are never fabricated - and unknown upstream fields are dropped.\n\nGenerated from services/social-data-skills/catalog/catalog_appstore.json (#16); do not edit by hand."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.replynodes.com",
      "description": "Use https://api.replynodes.com as the ReplyNodes fetcher gateway base URL."
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "bearerAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "appstore",
      "description": "Public App Store read operations."
    }
  ],
